2. Binaries in the repository
-----------------------------

RW612 Zephyr prover images (the first, single-image prover; release 0.1.0 and its deliberately tampered copy). They
are built from endpoints/rw612/prover and also contain, compiled in: the Zephyr RTOS (Apache-2.0), the MCUXpresso
SDK drivers for the RW612 (BSD-3-Clause), mldsa-native v2.0.0 and mlkem-native v2.0.0 (Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT).
  endpoints/rw612/artifacts/aegis-rw612-prover-0.1.0.bin
  endpoints/rw612/artifacts/aegis-rw612-prover-0.1.0.hex
  endpoints/rw612/artifacts/aegis-rw612-prover-0.1.0-tampered.bin

(The STM32 images are listed by checksum only in endpoints/stm32h573/artifacts/SHA256SUMS; the images themselves
are not in the repository.)


3. Data and figures
-------------------

NIST ACVP test vectors: not stored here. vectors/acvp/SHA256SUMS pins the files that tools/fetch_acvp.sh downloads
from the ACVP-Server repository (tag v1.1.0.41, vectors/acvp/SOURCE.txt).

docs/figures/ and the screenshot embedded in docs/diagrams/libero-aegis2-canvas-annotated.svg are screenshots of the
Libero SoC design tool showing this project's design.


4. Fetched at build or test time, not shipped
---------------------------------------------

These are downloaded by tools/setup_host.sh, the build scripts or CI and are not part of the repository:
liboqs 0.16.0 (MIT, with components under their own licences), mldsa-native and mlkem-native v2.0.0
(Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT), Trusted Firmware-M (BSD-3-Clause), Zephyr and the MCUXpresso SDK, STM32CubeH5,
